Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:05.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Breathing City is a Processing artwork that connects sound intensity to a Sydney Harbour
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.81,0:00:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,night scene. The bridge, opera-house shells, buildings, water and particles are drawn with code.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.13,0:00:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The intended interaction uses a microphone: gentle input produces a quieter city, while stronger
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.44,0:00:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,input produces brighter light and more motion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.50,0:00:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,This demonstration uses labelled synthetic input in the running sketch.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.64,0:00:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It shows calm, gentle, strong and recovery states, but it is not evidence of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.44,0:00:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,a person breathing into a microphone. Mouse simulation is also available.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.99,0:00:38.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The real microphone path uses the Processing Sound library.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.72,0:00:44.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It responds to loudness, so speech and other sounds can also activate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.50,0:00:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The first code section is SignalEnvelope. AudioIn captures the selected input channel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.05,0:00:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Amplitude calculates the root mean square of each audio block and returns a level.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.53,0:01:04.01,Default,,0,0,0,,During three seconds of calibration, the envelope collects room-noise readings and uses their ninetieth
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.01,0:01:09.10,Default,,0,0,0,,percentile. Staying quiet is important: sustained noise will raise this estimate.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.50,0:01:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The opening threshold adds an adjustable margin to the noise floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.44,0:01:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,A lower closing threshold creates hysteresis, reducing rapid on-off switching.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.92,0:01:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The signal above the opening threshold is multiplied by sensitivity and limited to zero
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.20,0:01:27.10,Default,,0,0,0,,through one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.50,0:01:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, exponential smoothing uses elapsed time. Its coefficient is one minus e to the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.78,0:01:41.06,Default,,0,0,0,,power of negative delta-time divided by tau. Attack takes a shorter time constant than
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.06,0:01:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,release, so the city responds quickly and settles gradually.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.50,0:01:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The second section is CityScene. One smoothed energy value controls several visible ranges.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.92,0:01:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Colour interpolation brightens windows, bridge lights and opera-house shells.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.36,0:02:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Wave phase accumulates speed multiplied by elapsed time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.31,0:02:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Stronger input increases both wave speed and amplitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.25,0:02:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Integrating phase avoids a sudden position jump when speed changes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.19,0:02:17.10,Default,,0,0,0,,This shared input makes the response coherent while each visual keeps its own scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.50,0:02:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The third section manages particles and ripples. Emission rate increases with energy, but particle
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.29,0:02:32.07,Default,,0,0,0,,count never exceeds one hundred and eighty. Ripples have a separate limit of eight.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.07,0:02:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Each object expires, and backward removal avoids skipped entries.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.44,0:02:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Ripple strength can rise after creation, preserving the difference between gentle and strong input
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.22,0:02:47.10,Default,,0,0,0,,instead of freezing strength near the trigger threshold.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.50,0:02:53.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The source, parameter guide, before-and-after files and test records accompany the project.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.59,0:02:59.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Hardware-specific microphone checks and real peer feedback remain separate from this simulated\Ndemonstration.
